# Glasgow service environment file -- example template.
#
# Copy this file to ONE of:
#
#   /etc/glasgow-svc.env       Production. Referenced by glasgow-svc.service
#                              via EnvironmentFile=. `sudo chmod 600` it.
#
#   deploy/glasgow-svc.env     Local development. Auto-discovered by
#                              glasgow_service.config.find_config_path so
#                              `uvicorn glasgow_service.api:app` and
#                              `pytest tests/test_wet_run.py` both pick
#                              it up with no extra exports. Add this path
#                              to .gitignore.
#
# You can also point at an arbitrary location with:
#   export GLASGOW_ENV_FILE=/some/other/path.env

# --- required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Absolute path to your streamData.json
GLASGOW_CONFIG=/home/vboxuser/Project/IobeamTech/Development/GlasgowDataIO/Json/streamData.json

# --- optional ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Bearer token for the REST endpoints. Leave commented out to run open
# on localhost; set it to require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
# Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# GLASGOW_TOKEN=replace-me-with-32-bytes-of-hex

# Require every mutating vacuum request to carry the elected executor's
# X-Executor-ID, X-Fencing-Token, and X-Lease-Valid-For-Ms headers. When this
# is enabled the vacuum controller does not start until an authorized executor
# calls /vacuum/acquire.
# GLASGOW_REQUIRE_FENCING=true

# Durable highest-token record used to reject stale leaders after service or
# host restart. The service account must be able to create this file and its
# parent directory.
# GLASGOW_FENCING_STATE=/var/lib/glasgow-service/fencing-token.json
